  "title": "Days and telling time",
  "note": "\"On\" a day is w + accusative: w poniedziałek, w środę, w sobotę (w becomes we before some clusters: we wtorek, we czwartek). Clock times use feminine ordinals because godzina (hour) is feminine: o pierwszej (at one), o drugiej (at two), o trzeciej (at three).",
  "src": {
    "t": "Oscar E. Swan, Polish-English Dictionary (University of Pittsburgh)",
    "u": "https://lektorek.org/polish/"
  },
